.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-PASSMENU 1 "2026-07-16" "paperweight-secrets 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-passmenu \- wofi picker for pass(1) entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-passmenu
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-passmenu
lists password entries in a
.BR wofi (1)
menu and copies the selected password to the clipboard, clearing it again
after 45 seconds (only if the clipboard still holds that exact value).
.PP
Two kinds of entries are listed together:
.TP
.B regular pass(1) entries
shown by their path, e.g.
.IR Applications/example .
.TP
.B app\-created secrets
entries created by another application through
.BR pass\-secret\-service (1)
(e.g. a browser saving a login), shown prefixed with a lock icon and
their D\-Bus
.I Label
instead of their internal id.
.PP
Entries mirrored into
.I secret_service/cli_mirror/
by
.BR paperweight\-secrets\-sync (1)
are not listed a second time under their mirror id \(em they already
appear once, under their original path.
.PP
A second invocation while one is already running (e.g. a repeated
$mod+p press before the first has finished) is ignored rather than
started concurrently \(em
.BR gpg\-agent (1)
only allows one live pinentry session at a time, so racing invocations
would otherwise fail unpredictably.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 if no entry is selected (Escape) or on success.
Exits 1 if the password store is missing or decryption fails, after
sending a desktop notification.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.password-store
The pass(1) store, or
.I $PASSWORD_STORE_DIR
if set.
.TP
.I ~/.password-store/secret_service/*/*.properties
Read to look up the
.I Label
of app\-created secrets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/paperweight-os/passmenu.log
Timestamped log of each run: entries found, selection, decrypt timing,
and any error output from
.BR pass (1).
Rotated at 1000 lines. Mode 600 \(em entry paths can be revealing even
though passwords themselves are never logged.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/paperweight-os/passmenu.lock
Concurrency-guard lock file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pass (1),
.BR paperweight\-secrets\-init (1),
.BR paperweight\-secrets\-sync (1)
